type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-2bcc32c3-7dac-5043-8989-0510498a8612" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9239ecfb-0eca-5feb-ad3c-12cda3308896" "answer-2bcc32c3-7dac-5043-8989-0510498a8612"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9239ecfb-0eca-5feb-ad3c-12cda3308896" :answer/id #uuid "9239ecfb-0eca-5feb-ad3c-12cda3308896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|U|=|V|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bcc32c3-7dac-5043-8989-0510498a8612" :answer/id #uuid "2bcc32c3-7dac-5043-8989-0510498a8612" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|U|\\ne |V|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d1a3ce27-2b7c-51c0-8626-2bd58e3fc009" :question/id #uuid "d1a3ce27-2b7c-51c0-8626-2bd58e3fc009" :question/math-academy-id "q-181629" :question/problem "$$\nC={1,2,…,100},\\,D={2n∣\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $C$ and $D$ above:" :question/worked-solution "The cardinalities of two sets cannot be equal if one set is finite and the other is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, notice that \n\n- $C$ is finite where $|C|=100,$  while\n\n- $D={…,-4,-2,0,2,4,…}$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, $|C|\\ne |D|.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a0ec03f8-a92e-5fcd-9e55-d8243fc6103d" "answer-field-bdccc4c7-e60a-5232-b424-539b4a705b10" "answer-field-9ed9cf7e-3305-561c-9635-f0b01605b2ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0ec03f8-a92e-5fcd-9e55-d8243fc6103d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ec03f8-a92e-5fcd-9e55-d8243fc6103d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-992ae3cd-1323-53e8-9ec4-b9fa1677154c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-992ae3cd-1323-53e8-9ec4-b9fa1677154c" "answer-64716a47-ff5f-564f-9df7-41f1fb56fa1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-992ae3cd-1323-53e8-9ec4-b9fa1677154c" :answer/id #uuid "992ae3cd-1323-53e8-9ec4-b9fa1677154c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "finite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64716a47-ff5f-564f-9df7-41f1fb56fa1c" :answer/id #uuid "64716a47-ff5f-564f-9df7-41f1fb56fa1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "infinite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bdccc4c7-e60a-5232-b424-539b4a705b10" :answer-field/id #uuid "bdccc4c7-e60a-5232-b424-539b4a705b10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c7ed87bb-bda0-579d-b12f-b02839095197" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3771c69-e53a-53ac-9fc8-43d408461163" "answer-c7ed87bb-bda0-579d-b12f-b02839095197"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3771c69-e53a-53ac-9fc8-43d408461163" :answer/id #uuid "a3771c69-e53a-53ac-9fc8-43d408461163" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "finite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7ed87bb-bda0-579d-b12f-b02839095197" :answer/id #uuid "c7ed87bb-bda0-579d-b12f-b02839095197" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "infinite" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ed9cf7e-3305-561c-9635-f0b01605b2ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ed9cf7e-3305-561c-9635-f0b01605b2ee" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-61d35919-3d71-5f27-bc47-e2a4c8bb3f47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b8f14f15-d965-5866-b818-dfd2f149c8f4" "answer-61d35919-3d71-5f27-bc47-e2a4c8bb3f47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8f14f15-d965-5866-b818-dfd2f149c8f4" :answer/id #uuid "b8f14f15-d965-5866-b818-dfd2f149c8f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|C|=|D|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61d35919-3d71-5f27-bc47-e2a4c8bb3f47" :answer/id #uuid "61d35919-3d71-5f27-bc47-e2a4c8bb3f47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|C|\\ne |D|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-99114540-20ff-5212-8b42-4abfffd44d45" :question/id #uuid "99114540-20ff-5212-8b42-4abfffd44d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-216536" :question/problem "$$\nA=N,\\,B={7,6,5,4,…}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $A$ and $B$ above:" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ have the *same cardinality* if there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nNotice that the elements of $B$ form an (infinite) arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =-1 \\\\  & =6-7 \\\\  & =5-6 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${b}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =7+(n-1)(-1) \\\\  & =7-n+1 \\\\  & =8-n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $B$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nB={8-n∣\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider the function $f:A\\to B$ that maps the underlying sets as follows: \n\n| $A$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $n$ | $⋯$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $B$ | $7$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $8-n$ | $⋯$ |\n\nIn general, for each $n\\in A,$ we have $f(n)=8-n\\in B.$\n\nNotice that $f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $B$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $A$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3439fa45-df35-559c-87d2-3593ce45fa38" "answer-field-d0a68429-9734-5c7e-8d07-fdbc30c08f75" "answer-field-2c50d1a9-abf6-5506-a4b6-cfd8e22e403c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3439fa45-df35-559c-87d2-3593ce45fa38" :answer-field/id #uuid "3439fa45-df35-559c-87d2-3593ce45fa38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9ffdd617-3b0c-5c42-98d8-d8baef5f7c0a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2234333-c812-5b7f-bc56-79b9f219a60b" "answer-9ffdd617-3b0c-5c42-98d8-d8baef5f7c0a" "answer-665b5365-d1bc-52ed-b375-56ea5f15c8c2" "answer-0e48d6d5-4b2c-52a8-9a4b-c369ffbce36c" "answer-ff462f97-882c-53fc-b113-f071b9188c16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2234333-c812-5b7f-bc56-79b9f219a60b" :answer/id #uuid "d2234333-c812-5b7f-bc56-79b9f219a60b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\cdot (-1)^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ffdd617-3b0c-5c42-98d8-d8baef5f7c0a" :answer/id #uuid "9ffdd617-3b0c-5c42-98d8-d8baef5f7c0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8-n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-665b5365-d1bc-52ed-b375-56ea5f15c8c2" :answer/id #uuid "665b5365-d1bc-52ed-b375-56ea5f15c8c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e48d6d5-4b2c-52a8-9a4b-c369ffbce36c" :answer/id #uuid "0e48d6d5-4b2c-52a8-9a4b-c369ffbce36c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{6}^{n}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff462f97-882c-53fc-b113-f071b9188c16" :answer/id #uuid "ff462f97-882c-53fc-b113-f071b9188c16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{8}^{n}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d0a68429-9734-5c7e-8d07-fdbc30c08f75" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a68429-9734-5c7e-8d07-fdbc30c08f75" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4442bb7f-b9f8-5131-87ad-ad385977ee90" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4442bb7f-b9f8-5131-87ad-ad385977ee90" "answer-f2ddebf6-21b6-508f-8caa-d9122038de83" "answer-160d8448-de95-5ab5-b208-5349c6f04cc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4442bb7f-b9f8-5131-87ad-ad385977ee90" :answer/id #uuid "4442bb7f-b9f8-5131-87ad-ad385977ee90" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "bijection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2ddebf6-21b6-508f-8caa-d9122038de83" :answer/id #uuid "f2ddebf6-21b6-508f-8caa-d9122038de83" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "injection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-160d8448-de95-5ab5-b208-5349c6f04cc0" :answer/id #uuid "160d8448-de95-5ab5-b208-5349c6f04cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "surjection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c50d1a9-abf6-5506-a4b6-cfd8e22e403c" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c50d1a9-abf6-5506-a4b6-cfd8e22e403c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-37f43ebd-0002-534a-b66a-2daa040139df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-37f43ebd-0002-534a-b66a-2daa040139df" "answer-2ad6fb88-5156-5ca7-a2bc-92460ffef6b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37f43ebd-0002-534a-b66a-2daa040139df" :answer/id #uuid "37f43ebd-0002-534a-b66a-2daa040139df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ad6fb88-5156-5ca7-a2bc-92460ffef6b6" :answer/id #uuid "2ad6fb88-5156-5ca7-a2bc-92460ffef6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e32b700f-379c-5d3a-b0db-4859531b5dcb" :question/id #uuid "e32b700f-379c-5d3a-b0db-4859531b5dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-181743" :question/problem "$$\nA={5,7,9,11,…},\\,B=N\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $A$ and $B$ (shown above):" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ have the *same cardinality* if there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nNotice that the elements of $A$ form an (infinite) arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =9-7 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =5+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nA={2n+3∣\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider the function $f:B\\to A$ that maps the underlying sets as follows: \n\n| $B$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $n$ | $⋯$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $A$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ | $⋯$ | $2n+3$ | $⋯$ |\n\nIn general, for each $n\\in B,$ we have $f(n)=2n+3\\in A.$\n\nNotice that $f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $A$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $B$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b17d837-2804-5565-af89-19f792fb3dd3" "answer-field-84b7562f-be27-5aff-94f5-a3eb063ffd99" "answer-field-ab4a98f8-d784-53be-8554-ae2490cbe22d" "answer-field-5c17b3d7-202b-5319-afd9-fd4e982a5f27"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b17d837-2804-5565-af89-19f792fb3dd3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b17d837-2804-5565-af89-19f792fb3dd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c509085e-6a08-5784-94d6-5dc99ca56924" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c509085e-6a08-5784-94d6-5dc99ca56924" "answer-61731695-4507-53d3-8c18-99d25efe6709" "answer-16d4a2f9-e593-5566-822b-84853d2f0ef4" "answer-26796553-8f80-51bc-9a2e-35ca8a8cb416" "answer-109421d6-88fa-52a8-974a-f85b7d91314e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c509085e-6a08-5784-94d6-5dc99ca56924" :answer/id #uuid "c509085e-6a08-5784-94d6-5dc99ca56924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2n+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61731695-4507-53d3-8c18-99d25efe6709" :answer/id #uuid "61731695-4507-53d3-8c18-99d25efe6709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3n+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16d4a2f9-e593-5566-822b-84853d2f0ef4" :answer/id #uuid "16d4a2f9-e593-5566-822b-84853d2f0ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26796553-8f80-51bc-9a2e-35