ey "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" "answer-2d5712b5-5792-554d-8f40-73fe534ecc0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer/id #uuid "81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d5712b5-5792-554d-8f40-73fe534ecc0b" :answer/id #uuid "2d5712b5-5792-554d-8f40-73fe534ecc0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172390 :question/problem "$$\nA={3,6,12,24,…},\\,B=N\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $A$ and $B$ (shown above):" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ have the *same cardinality* if there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nNotice that the elements of $A$ form an (infinite) geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nA={3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}∣\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider the function $f:B\\to A$ that maps the underlying sets as follows: \n\n| $B$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $n$ | $⋯$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $A$ | $3$ | $6$ | $12$ | $24$ | $⋯$ | $3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}$ | $⋯$ |\n\nIn general, for each $n\\in B,$ we have $f(n)=3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}\\in A.$\n\nNotice that $f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $A$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $B$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af555a01-5a46-56eb-990a-f86aa1f4392b" "answer-field-b7976db9-2db5-5508-b5c5-470334703fc9" "answer-field-226a71c8-8ee0-5ede-b4fb-4602d14e2399" "answer-field-b5e830d8-4775-54a6-8f79-f32d4be3ba87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af555a01-5a46-56eb-990a-f86aa1f4392b" :answer-field/id #uuid "af555a01-5a46-56eb-990a-f86aa1f4392b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-d8380d51-6839-56f7-aca1-b953369cebd1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-26e5060e-a47f-5148-b58b-7f347b027a64" "answer-d8380d51-6839-56f7-aca1-b953369cebd1" "answer-730bdc07-19a7-515b-a282-86cf593fa9fd" "answer-db7c03a5-d525-5ab5-89bb-e3868d5e36e0" "answer-cffe121f-d0d3-573d-8166-b80e543428bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26e5060e-a47f-5148-b58b-7f347b027a64" :answer/id #uuid "26e5060e-a47f-5148-b58b-7f347b027a64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot {3}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8380d51-6839-56f7-aca1-b953369cebd1" :answer/id #uuid "d8380d51-6839-56f7-aca1-b953369cebd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-730bdc07-19a7-515b-a282-86cf593fa9fd" :answer/id #uuid "730bdc07-19a7-515b-a282-86cf593fa9fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db7c03a5-d525-5ab5-89bb-e3868d5e36e0" :answer/id #uuid "db7c03a5-d525-5ab5-89bb-e3868d5e36e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3n+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cffe121f-d0d3-573d-8166-b80e543428bc" :answer/id #uuid "cffe121f-d0d3-573d-8166-b80e543428bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7976db9-2db5-5508-b5c5-470334703fc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7976db9-2db5-5508-b5c5-470334703fc9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-03ddee33-7744-5ed1-9e92-d7aa8dfc6ad3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e237efc1-efd8-5f4f-94ad-18272b4fb940" "answer-03ddee33-7744-5ed1-9e92-d7aa8dfc6ad3" "answer-12e35f19-ae43-50ea-84ae-332c8e379c47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e237efc1-efd8-5f4f-94ad-18272b4fb940" :answer/id #uuid "e237efc1-efd8-5f4f-94ad-18272b4fb940" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03ddee33-7744-5ed1-9e92-d7aa8dfc6ad3" :answer/id #uuid "03ddee33-7744-5ed1-9e92-d7aa8dfc6ad3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "injective" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12e35f19-ae43-50ea-84ae-332c8e379c47" :answer/id #uuid "12e35f19-ae43-50ea-84ae-332c8e379c47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "positive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-226a71c8-8ee0-5ede-b4fb-4602d14e2399" :answer-field/id #uuid "226a71c8-8ee0-5ede-b4fb-4602d14e2399" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3ab8a727-abd6-5eee-91b1-5176578c7a08" :answer-field/choices ["answer-996e8f12-3b45-562f-a82b-60cba4333d69" "answer-eef5fb9c-5d39-552a-8b38-51c6a497a262" "answer-3ab8a727-abd6-5eee-91b1-5176578c7a08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-996e8f12-3b45-562f-a82b-60cba4333d69" :answer/id #uuid "996e8f12-3b45-562f-a82b-60cba4333d69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "increasing" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eef5fb9c-5d39-552a-8b38-51c6a497a262" :answer/id #uuid "eef5fb9c-5d39-552a-8b38-51c6a497a262" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ab8a727-abd6-5eee-91b1-5176578c7a08" :answer/id #uuid "3ab8a727-abd6-5eee-91b1-5176578c7a08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "surjective" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5e830d8-4775-54a6-8f79-f32d4be3ba87" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e830d8-4775-54a6-8f79-f32d4be3ba87" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-fe3c1429-9fec-53d1-8796-cb7d78667725" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fe3c1429-9fec-53d1-8796-cb7d78667725" "answer-326dcf9c-7c4f-56da-87bf-d4b8c35be676"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe3c1429-9fec-53d1-8796-cb7d78667725" :answer/id #uuid "fe3c1429-9fec-53d1-8796-cb7d78667725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-326dcf9c-7c4f-56da-87bf-d4b8c35be676" :answer/id #uuid "326dcf9c-7c4f-56da-87bf-d4b8c35be676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f930f3c4-3dbb-5481-a48e-987b268b6aa0" :question/id #uuid "f930f3c4-3dbb-5481-a48e-987b268b6aa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-216560" :question/problem "$$\nA={27,9,3,1,…},\\,B=N\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $A$ and $B$ (shown above):" :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ have the *same cardinality* if there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nNotice that the elements of $A$ form an (infinite) geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{9} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =27{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nA={27{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n-1}\\,|\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider the function $f:B\\to A$ that maps the underlying sets as follows: \n\n| $B$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $n$ | $⋯$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $A$ | $27$ | $9$ | $3$ | $1$ | $⋯$ | $27{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n-1}$ | $⋯$ |\n\nIn general, for each $n\\in B,$ we have $f(n)=27{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n-1}\\in A.$\n\nNotice that $f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $A$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $B$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be0b2b0a-b1be-5c67-a5f6-cae22d0082d9" "answer-field-ac921dd5-690c-58f0-8b02-be8446969778" "answer-field-0ecdd120-3ad6-57f9-b83b-764594ebf2c7" "answer-field-ebba6751-55d0-5779-b8c6-94ff7e2af4f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be0b2b0a-b1be-5c67-a5f6-cae22d0082d9" :answer-field/id #uuid "be0b2b0a-b1be-5c67-a5f6-cae22d0082d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a4762cd9-7c46-5f46-bcad-49db5dd4b299" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4762cd9-7c46-5f46-bcad-49db5dd4b299" "answer-1ae08d50-549a-553f-80ff-d96ebd123adb" "answer-b29534ff-2ae7-585d-8881-b3d42ee5a597" "answer-b09527f8-5a98-5706-94e0-30faeab70cfc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4762cd9-7c46-5f46-bcad-49db5dd4b299" :answer/id #uuid "a4762cd9-7c46-5f46-bcad-49db5dd4b299" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ae08d50-549a-553f-80ff-d96ebd123adb" :answer/id #uuid "1ae08d50-549a-553f-80ff-d96ebd123adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b29534ff-2ae7-585d-8881-b3d42ee5a597" :answer/id #uuid "b29534ff-2ae7-585d-8881-b3d42ee5a597" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{n-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09527f8-5a98-5706-94e0-30faeab70cfc" :answer/id #uuid "b09527f8-5a98-5706-94e0-30faeab70cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac921dd5-690c-58f0-8b02-be8446969778" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac921dd5-690c-58f0-8b02-be8446969778" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-cadc129c-da1e-5e62-bc75-cc7df4bcec00" :answer-field/choices ["answer-23945915-4c04-59b5-9258-20a54b3f1b8d" "answer-cadc129c-da1e-5e62-bc75-cc7df4bcec00" "answer-5ee305bc-7787-5d82-a06a-107208f20ed1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23945915-4c04-59b5-9258-20a54b3f1b8d" :answer/id #uuid "23945915-4c04-59b5-9258-20a54b3f1b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cadc129c-da1e-5e62-bc75-cc7df4bcec00" :answer/id #uuid "cadc129c-da1e-5e62-bc75-cc7df4bcec00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "injective" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ee305bc-7787-5d82-a06a-107208f20ed1" :answer/id #uuid "5ee305bc-7787-5d82-a06a-107208f20ed1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "positive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0ecdd120-3ad6-57f9-b83b-764594ebf2c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecdd120-3ad6-57f9-b83b-764594ebf2c7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ab0679db-895a-5a46-9a05-9b44fb8f1e1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d98081a8-2046-5b75-ac9e-78b3fc9d7683" "answer-b51f41ec-ff36-5e1c-ac65-318bd0b22be8" "answer-ab0679db-895a-5a46-9a05-9b44fb8f1e1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d98081a8-2046-5b75-ac9e-78b3fc9d7683" :answer/id #uuid "d98081a8-2046-5b75-ac9e-78b3fc9d7683" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "increasing" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b51f41ec-ff36-5e1c-ac65-318bd0b22be8" :answer/id #uuid "b51f41ec-ff36-5e1c-ac65-318bd0b22be8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrable" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab0679db-895a-5a46-9a05-9b44fb8f1e1f" :answer/id #uuid "ab0679db-895a-5a46-9a05-9b44fb8f1e1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "surjective" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ebba6751-55d0-5779-b8c6-94ff7e2af4f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebba6751-55d0-5779-b8c6-94ff7e2af4f7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ee6aeca2-f6d4-5e51-a143-cdabedf162f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ee6aeca2-f6d4-5e51-a143-cdabedf162f0" "answer-03306edf-541c-55bb-bdc4-0c703c1cce39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee6aeca2-f6d4-5e51-a143-cdabedf162f0" :answer/id #uuid "ee6aeca2-f6d4-5e51-a143-cdabedf162f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03306edf-541c-55bb-bdc4-0c703c1cce39" :answer/id #uuid "03306edf-541c-55bb-bdc4-0c703c1cce39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173263 :tutorial/content "We recently defined two *finite* sets $A$ and $B$ as having the *same cardinality* if they contain the same number of elements. \n\nWhile this might seem a reasonable definition, we'd like to extend the concept of cardinality to infinite sets. Unfortunately, this definition will not do since counting the elements of an infinite set is impossible. \n\nTo get around this difficulty, we need a revised definition. Here it is:\n\n*Two set $A$ and $B$ have the **same cardinality** if there exists a bijection of $A$ onto $B.$ In other words, there is a one-to-one correspondence between the elements of the sets. Otherwise, if no such bijection exists, the sets are said to have **unequal cardinalities**.*\n\nAs before, we write $|A|= |B|$ when $A$ and $B$ have equal cardinalities, and $|A|\\neq |B|$ otherwise.\n\nFor finite sets, the situation is pretty simple. If two sets $A$ and $B$ have equal cardinality, then there exists a mapping that uniquely pairs each element of $A$ with an element of $B.$ This is equivalent to saying that $A$ and $B$ contain the same number of elements. \n\nFor example, the sets $A = \\{ a,b,c, d \\}$ and $B = \\{ 0, 1, 2, 3 \\}$ each have a cardinality of $4.$ The corresponding bijection might be the following:\n\n![](images/d8/d8d2c9de97d811be0e38ec1512546a399ebc3ee299934746a8d47bf30354b7b1.png)\n\n   \n\nIn contrast, for the sets $C = \\{ \\triangle \\}$ and $D = \\{ \\clubsuit, \\spadesuit \\},$ no bijections exist between these sets since they have different numbers of elements. Therefore, they have unequal cardinalities.\n\nFor infinite sets, it's a bit more complicated. However, we have the following fact to get us started:\n\n*If a set $A$ is finite and another set $B$ is infinite, then these sets have unequal cardinalities.*" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172199 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
